msgstr "An `oklch(from …)` expression resolving to black or white."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/overlayColors.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# Function: overlayColors()"
msgstr "# Funksjon: overlayColors()"

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/overlayColors.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Flatten `overlay` (at `percent`% strength) over an opaque `base` — a CSS-only stand-in for\nui-color-utils `overlayColors`. That helper source-over-composites two RGBA colors into one opaque\nresult; the common case (a translucent tint over a solid surface) is exactly a two-color\n`color-mix()`. General RGBA-over-RGBA compositing can't be a single CSS color, so this covers the\nopaque-base case only."
msgstr "Flatten `overlay` (at `percent`% strength) over an opaque `base` — a CSS-only stand-in for\nui-color-utils `overlayColors`. That helper source-over-composites two RGBA colors into one opaque\nresult; the common case (a translucent tint over a solid surface) is exactly a two-color\n`color-mix()`. General RGBA-over-RGBA compositing can't be a single CSS color, so this covers the\nopaque-base case only."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/overlayColors.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The opaque background color."
msgstr "The opaque background color."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/overlayColors.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "### overlay"
msgstr "### overlay"

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/overlayColors.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The color laid over it."
msgstr "The color laid over it."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/overlayColors.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "How much of `overlay` shows through, 0–100 (default `50`)."
msgstr "How much of `overlay` shows through, 0–100 (default `50`)."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# colors"
msgstr "# colors"

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`@pantoken/plugin-colors` — CSS-only color math that mirrors the InstUI `@instructure/ui-color-utils`\nhelpers (`alpha`, `darken`, `lighten`, `overlayColors`)."
msgstr "`@pantoken/plugin-colors` — CSS-only color math that mirrors the InstUI `@instructure/ui-color-utils`\nhelpers (`alpha`, `darken`, `lighten`, `overlayColors`)."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "InstUI computes those at build time with `tinycolor2` against concrete hex values. pantoken emits\n`var(--instui-*)` references that resolve in the browser (often through `light-dark()`), so the\nmath has to happen in CSS instead. Each helper returns a CSS color string built from\n[`color-mix()`](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/CSS/color_value/color-mix) and\n[relative color syntax](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_colors/Relative_colors) —\nboth Baseline modern-browser features — so a single expression tracks the token even when it's a\nscheme-dependent `light-dark()` pair. Use them wherever you'd otherwise hard-code a derived shade."
msgstr "InstUI computes those at build time with `tinycolor2` against concrete hex values. pantoken emits\n`var(--instui-*)` references that resolve in the browser (often through `light-dark()`), so the\nmath has to happen in CSS instead. Each helper returns a CSS color string built from\n[`color-mix()`](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/CSS/color_value/color-mix) and\n[relative color syntax](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_colors/Relative_colors) —\nboth Baseline modern-browser features — so a single expression tracks the token even when it's a\nscheme-dependent `light-dark()` pair. Use them wherever you'd otherwise hard-code a derived shade."

